            <ArticleTitle>Is it acute cholecystitis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a prospective study of 100 patients presenting with acute right hypochondrial pain and diagnosed clinically by a qualified surgeon as having acute cholecystitis, we have shown that the diagnostic error can be considerable. Twenty-five of these patients were found to have a different diagnosis on subsequent investigation and in a further 11 patients, no definite diagnosis could be established. This emphasises the need for careful investigation of patients with this presenting complaint.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
